8.11 NCIC NOTIFICATION (Reports)
8.11.1 REPORTS REQUIRING NCIC NOTIFICATION
A Louisville Metro Police Department (LMPD) officer, Police Report Technician (PRT), or LMPD Service Center Technician will report the following to the National Crime Information Center (NCIC) Unit prior to clearing from the call for service (KACP 26.3, 26.4):
• Missing persons (refer to SOP 8.32);
• Stolen or recovered vehicles (including carjackings);
• Stolen or recovered construction equipment and trailers;
• Stolen/lost/recovered guns with known serial numbers;
• Stolen or recovered boats;
• Stolen or recovered securities;
• Stolen or recovered license plates;
• Vehicle/boat parts with unique serial numbers; and/or
• Stolen or recovered articles not listed above, with known serial numbers or unique owner-applied numbers, which have a value of $500 or more.
Before a member reports a vehicle as stolen, they are required to check the Records Management System (RMS) to ensure that the vehicle has not been towed first.
8.11.2 STOLEN OR LOST VEHICLES/PERSONS/ITEMS REQUIRING NCIC NOTIFICATION
Upon completion of the report for stolen or lost vehicle/person/item and when there is enough information to complete the NCIC notification, the member must, prior to clearing the call for service:
• Export a copy of the report, open, and print to the NCIC Unit, through the RMS, and follow-up by calling the NCIC Unit to verify that the report was received; or
• Call the NCIC Unit at (502) 572-3480 if they are unable to immediately print a copy of the report to the NCIC Unit, through the RMS; or
• Convert the report to a PDF and email it to contactncic@louisvilleky.gov.
Once the member has sent NCIC a copy of the report, the member will do the following:
• Call the NCIC Unit by phone at (502) 572-3480 and verify they received a copy of the report.
• Obtain the name and code number of the NCIC Unit operator to whom they spoke.
• Enter the following information into the investigative narrative section of the incident report:
o NCIC Unit operator’s name and code number o Date and time the NCIC Unit operator was notified
If the above information is not included, the report will be sent back for correction.
8.11.3 RECOVERY OF STOLEN OR LOST VEHICLES/ITEMS REQUIRING NCIC NOTIFICATION
All identifiable stolen property, including stolen vehicles, recovered as a result of an RMS or NCIC “hit,” must be verified through the service channel before it can be seized/recovered. The RMS will not automatically send this information to the NCIC Unit. It is the responsibility of the reporting member to verify that the NCIC Unit is notified.
It will be the responsibility of the member who recovered the stolen property to obtain the rightful property owner’s information (e.g., name, address, telephone number). Ownership may be obtained through the RMS or by obtaining the original stolen property report from an outside originating agency. The member may request assistance from the NCIC Unit with obtaining stolen property reports from outside originating agencies. However, it is the recovering member’s responsibility to obtain information regarding the rightful owner of the stolen property. The member will enter the owner’s information into the RMS.
The member who has recovered a stolen vehicle will attempt to contact the victim who reported the vehicle stolen. The member will notate who they called on the Incident Modifying Supplement (IMS) report, the number they called, and the disposition of the phone call (refer to SOP 8.11.4).
8.11.4 RECOVERY OF STOLEN OR LOST ITEMS REQUIRING NCIC NOTIFICATION WITHIN LMPD JURISDICTION
In cases where the original stolen/lost report was taken by the LMPD, the recovering member is responsible for completing an IMS report within the RMS with, at a minimum, the following information:
• Pertinent details of the recovery should be listed in the narrative of the IMS;
• Add new status of the property as “recovered,” if originally stolen, or “found,” if originally lost;
• Date, time, and location of the recovery should be included in the property or vehicle card;
• Prior to approving the IMS with the above information, the member will print the recovery/cancellation supplement to the NCIC Unit printer, or convert the report to PDF and email it to contactncic@louisvilleky.gov;
• The member will immediately call the NCIC Unit at (502) 572-3480 to verify that the IMS was received;
• The member will include the NCIC Unit operator’s name and code number to whom they verified the receipt of the IMS and include this information in the IMS narrative;
• The member will then approve the IMS for further review.
Local recoveries with a local arrest made should also include:
• The original report should remain Theft by Unlawful Taking (TBUT); however, the suspect should be charged on the citation with Receiving Stolen Property (RSP), unless the officer has established probable cause for the TBUT charge.
o If charging TBUT, add suspect information through an IMS. o If charging RSP, add the suspect information and RSP offense through an IMS.
